<title>CANADA: CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - Dec 17.</title>
<headline>CAODC weekly western Canadian rig count - Dec 17.</headline>
<text>
<p>WEEK OF DECEMBER 17 VERSUS DECEMBER 10, 1996	   DRILLING</p>
<p>	     MOVING  RIGGING  DRILLING   DOWN    TOTAL   YR AGO</p>
<p> ALBERTA    1/10    0/1     333/311   16/26   350/348    263</p>
<p> SASK.	1/3     0/0	75/78     1/2     77/83	38</p>
<p> B.C.	 0/2     0/0	43/34     2/4     45/40	31</p>
<p> N.W.T.     0/0     0/0	 1/0	4/4	5/4	  1</p>
<p> MAN.	 0/0     0/0	 2/2	0/0	2/2	  1</p>
<p> TOTAL	2/15    0/1     454/425   23/36   479/477    334</p>
<p>MOVING, RIGGING = CURRENTLY UNDER CONTRACT, BUT NOT AT FULL RATE. TOTAL LINE IS TOTAL WESTERN CANADA. FIGURES SUPPLIED BY CANADIAN ASSOCIATION OF OILWELL DRILLING CONTRACTORS.</p>
<p>-- Calgary Bureau (403) 531-1624</p>
